{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","id":"pg_5da4609005ba5fe7ba3d66ec4a781472","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sanbuphy-learn-coding-agent-docs-en-02-hidden-features-and-codenames-m-66ec4a781472.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_220646613dad5cee9cf548759d9cf00f"],"title":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent/docs/en/02-hidden-features-and-codenames.md @ ce8ca4a8e722","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","id":"pg_653c8e9171725786aa4eaae705cdb42e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sanbuphy-learn-coding-agent-docs-en-03-undercover-mode-md-ce8ca4a8e722-aae705cdb42e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1cb22edcc62e535db51a156689300463"],"title":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent/docs/en/03-undercover-mode.md @ ce8ca4a8e722","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e8bfce9495b6677b00fc54c44b5cfc111fa9b06ad8d718c703e015ba4e77650"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented design patterns include AsyncGenerator streaming through the query chain, a buildTool factory with safe defaults, compile-time feature-flag dead-code elimination via Bun, and AsyncLocalStorage for per-agent context isolation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_13c4763e188a75beb6a7d1ff4993baab7ef12093a1691476e620f9e1fc4200f9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each tool implements a documented lifecycle (validateInput, checkPermissions, call) plus capability predicates like isConcurrencySafe, isReadOnly, and isDestructive, and React/Ink renderers for tool use and results."},{"claim_ids":["clm_289f7e217cb42d4b90ced9a03d4cc02e101e176f17a834eac8729ed875ebec79"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is a learning/research project on CLI Agent architecture, compiled entirely from publicly available online references and discussions, focused on claude-code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2bcec3fd6c2c4d7cc3627e07188fd6d5d8b5e04f6262e02efbe134ac544436fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository's own disclaimer prohibits commercial use of its content and limits it to research and educational purposes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_32812d565baeb9f4522742a5f580623b19eb86f465ad1e78367d6d7cd8a398f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Context management uses three compression strategies: autoCompact (summarize old messages via an API call when tokens exceed a threshold), snipCompact, and contextCollapse, the latter two behind feature flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c620221a7fe310d14dcc0ec56ecad6ea03e245e0ec20d47f30c70ff745b2ab9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documentation frames Claude Code as a minimal agent loop (call API, check stop_reason for tool_use, execute tools, append results) wrapped by a production harness adding permissions, streaming, concurrency, compaction, sub-agents, persistence, and MCP."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5035704f2989db7dbda9e93d5e91ca3f9a958918e1be301f46b0002cae5b557d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The entry layer routes interactive use through a REPL and headless/SDK use through QueryEngine, whose submitMessage returns an AsyncGenerator of SDKMessages streamed to the consumer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_516b880a87f290c6a6159f98f743ffa4f4059fa8182bd1c3e99c7b41519e31a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented permission flow orders validateInput, user-defined PreToolUse hooks, always-allow/deny/ask rules from settings or CLI args, an interactive Allow Once/Always/Deny prompt, then tool-specific checkPermissions logic such as path sandboxing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5a723f86f5f1e5f2972d932cb59d1edeb4a1be1a955d0f184ff2780961896446"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation reports roughly 1,884 TS/TSX files, ~512,664 lines, ~40+ built-in tools, ~80+ slash commands, and a Bun runtime compiled to a Node.js >= 18 bundle."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e9ac9b3c2cf95db8d9311f007cbbd06316e46223a8000db1749ccaa0eef7308"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented dependency footprint is about 192 node_modules packages, with the runtime built on Bun and compiled to a Node.js >= 18 bundle."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b8b632b0e976d05802f39be926e0caf791fae40cc95d5686207835980b5e271d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sub-agents can spawn in four modes: default in-process with shared conversation, fork as a child process with fresh messages, worktree isolation, or remote via a bridge; agents communicate via SendMessageTool and a shared task board."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8541eab83c8b010786fcaaa446ac33204fa161c982648ba1c90baa6a7b0d58f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented source layout includes main.tsx (REPL bootstrap), QueryEngine.ts (headless/SDK lifecycle), query.ts (main agent loop, largest file), Tool.ts, tools.ts, commands.ts, and a bridge/ directory for Claude Desktop/remote sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ddc9ada0fdc8b6b0d57cfb5af467f512fac61f0ef4faa706de65a97ce526b45c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions persist as append-only JSONL under ~/.claude/projects/<hash>/sessions/, with resume options --continue, --resume <id>, and --fork-session; user messages are written blocking for crash recovery while assistant messages use a fire-and-forget queue."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fca552743ffad0fa79d056472d10066a7a576605b5635e86f990c59802ee42d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The analyzed target is Claude Code v2.1.88; reports cover telemetry, codenames, undercover mode, remote control, and a future roadmap."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0e8bfce9495b6677b00fc54c44b5cfc111fa9b06ad8d718c703e015ba4e77650","clm_13c4763e188a75beb6a7d1ff4993baab7ef12093a1691476e620f9e1fc4200f9","clm_289f7e217cb42d4b90ced9a03d4cc02e101e176f17a834eac8729ed875ebec79","clm_2bcec3fd6c2c4d7cc3627e07188fd6d5d8b5e04f6262e02efbe134ac544436fd","clm_32812d565baeb9f4522742a5f580623b19eb86f465ad1e78367d6d7cd8a398f0","clm_3c620221a7fe310d14dcc0ec56ecad6ea03e245e0ec20d47f30c70ff745b2ab9","clm_5035704f2989db7dbda9e93d5e91ca3f9a958918e1be301f46b0002cae5b557d","clm_516b880a87f290c6a6159f98f743ffa4f4059fa8182bd1c3e99c7b41519e31a2","clm_5a723f86f5f1e5f2972d932cb59d1edeb4a1be1a955d0f184ff2780961896446","clm_6e9ac9b3c2cf95db8d9311f007cbbd06316e46223a8000db1749ccaa0eef7308","clm_b8b632b0e976d05802f39be926e0caf791fae40cc95d5686207835980b5e271d","clm_c8541eab83c8b010786fcaaa446ac33204fa161c982648ba1c90baa6a7b0d58f","clm_ddc9ada0fdc8b6b0d57cfb5af467f512fac61f0ef4faa706de65a97ce526b45c","clm_fca552743ffad0fa79d056472d10066a7a576605b5635e86f990c59802ee42d8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","id":"pg_8f2d2cd0a86457abbeeb876dd247f069","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sanbuphy-learn-coding-agent-readme-md-ce8ca4a8e722-876dd247f069.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_eb3f68c4732e52deacd2194c84bee553"],"title":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent/